1
00:00:31,399 --> 00:00:33,359
If you had brought out that money

2
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,280
and laid it out in front of everyone,

3
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,640
telling them what happened that night,

4
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,399
would anyone still refuse to believe it?

5
00:00:42,119 --> 00:00:44,880
If Liu Tieping had known the truth,

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,560
would he have done something so stupid?

7
00:00:50,039 --> 00:00:51,920
If Qian Yichuan had known the truth,

8
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,679
would he have hurled insults at

9
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:56,159
such a kindhearted woman?

10
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,439
Every holiday,

11
00:01:01,479 --> 00:01:02,640
you throw money around,

12
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:04,359
visiting the weak and the sick.

13
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,799
But have you ever told them

14
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:10,159
that this money was won

15
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:11,799
by Liu Xuemei for them?

16
00:01:11,799 --> 00:01:14,079
That she drank for it, cup after cup?

17
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,599
If she hadn't been forced to drink,

18
00:01:22,319 --> 00:01:23,760
she wouldn't have frozen to death.

19
00:01:25,519 --> 00:01:27,319
If she'd known you were like this,

20
00:01:28,519 --> 00:01:30,480
she would've rather gone to Cheng Youtian

21
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,000
and wouldn't have frozen to death.

22
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:41,719
Liu Tieping killing someone was indeed a crime.

23
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,760
And what about you?

24
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:48,319
Isn't what you did a crime too?

25
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,239
Everyone says

26
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,760
you're a good person.

27
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,359
But in reality?

28
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:00,400
Have you ever searched your conscience?

29
00:02:01,959 --> 00:02:04,439
How can you face a soul misunderstood,

30
00:02:04,599 --> 00:02:05,719
slandered,

31
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:08,520
and stripped of dignity?

32
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,800
How can you face your own soul?

33
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:18,680
Did you deserve Liu Xuemei's trust?

34
00:02:29,159 --> 00:02:30,719
Are you even human?

35
00:02:36,039 --> 00:02:38,039
Are you even human?

36
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,240
Poor Sister Xuemei.

37
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,639
I heard

38
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,479
her kid is still pretty young.

39
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:14,680
Yeah.

40
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:20,400
When the time comes,

41
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,680
around the holidays and such,

42
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,159
we should go visit him,

43
00:03:25,759 --> 00:03:27,439
see if he's having any trouble,

44
00:03:27,439 --> 00:03:28,639
and help out however we can.

45
00:03:40,719 --> 00:03:41,560
Where's the money?

46
00:03:54,639 --> 00:03:55,159
I spent it.

47
00:04:03,719 --> 00:04:04,360
Actually,

48
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,800
every year during the holidays,

49
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,840
and for fellow workers' major life events,

50
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:17,120
I gave plenty of gift money.

51
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:20,560
Including for your mom.

52
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:37,120
Let's not talk about this anymore.

53
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,639
Tomorrow, I'll turn myself in to the police.

54
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:46,600
Whether they lock me up or fine me,

55
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,319
I'll take it all.

56
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,040
Hold on.

57
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,399
Explain yourself.

58
00:04:54,079 --> 00:04:55,120
What happened to my mom?

59
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:57,959
It's nothing.

60
00:04:58,639 --> 00:04:59,319
Explain yourself.

61
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:00,279
What happened to my mom?

62
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:07,120
Back in 2003,

63
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:11,959
didn't your mom get surgery for a pacemaker?

64
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,959
You were busy in Beijing back then,

65
00:05:16,079 --> 00:05:16,680
couldn't make it back.

66
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,519
I paid for it.

67
00:05:19,519 --> 00:05:20,040
No...

68
00:05:21,839 --> 00:05:22,959
What was actually used was

69
00:05:23,439 --> 00:05:24,199
Liu Xuemei's money.

70
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,439
Is there anything else?

71
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,319
In Beijing,

72
00:05:50,879 --> 00:05:52,040
your tuition,

73
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,360
living expenses,

74
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:55,879
and rent—

75
00:06:01,879 --> 00:06:02,639
it all came from Xuemei.

76
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,920
Back then, you never even asked me

77
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:46,240
where a laid-off worker like me got so much money.

78
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,360
I told you back then

79
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,079
I earned it from the bridal shop,

80
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,920
that I was sharper than everyone else,

81
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,199
and you just bought it.

82
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,480
Right.

83
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,360
The startup funds for that bridal shop...

84
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,199
came from Liu Xuemei.

85
00:07:03,199 --> 00:07:03,959
But the point is,

86
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,279
do you know, opening that shop,

87
00:07:06,279 --> 00:07:07,399
how much effort I put in?

88
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,079
I worked from dawn till dusk.

89
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,199
Dirty work, hard labor,

90
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,240
I did all of it.

91
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,240
And why?

92
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:16,720
Just so you could live a good life in Beijing!

93
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,160
I really didn't want to

94
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,399
tell you any of this.

95
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:31,879
Really.

96
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:33,240
I'd rather die than

97
00:07:33,279 --> 00:07:34,680
tell you about this.

98
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,160
Because I didn't want you to end up like me,

99
00:07:37,199 --> 00:07:38,319
carrying this burden of guilt.

100
00:07:41,439 --> 00:07:43,879
Just one wrong move,

101
00:07:46,959 --> 00:07:48,360
and there was no turning back.

102
00:07:50,639 --> 00:07:52,240
It's been sheer agony.

103
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,439
You know,

104
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:01,040
ever since I touched that money

105
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:03,040
and didn't turn it in,

106
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,000
I haven't been able to sleep.

107
00:08:06,879 --> 00:08:08,800
I keep having nightmares!

108
00:08:14,879 --> 00:08:16,199
I'd much rather

109
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,959
have nothing to my name,

110
00:08:18,959 --> 00:08:20,439
be dirt poor,

111
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,199
than have touched that money.

112
00:08:22,199 --> 00:08:23,399
I never should've touched it.

113
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,839
There's no going back.

114
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,320
There's no going back now...

115
00:08:46,919 --> 00:08:48,080
So Leshui, you see,

116
00:08:49,639 --> 00:08:50,200
that's just how it is.

117
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:51,960
I

118
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:54,120
might seem,

119
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,279
right?

120
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:56,840
like a pretty decent guy.

121
00:08:58,279 --> 00:08:59,799
But do you have any idea

122
00:08:59,799 --> 00:09:01,399
what kind of filth I hide inside?

123
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,360
And you're no different.

124
00:09:07,159 --> 00:09:08,120
Without even realizing it,

125
00:09:08,799 --> 00:09:11,320
you've been tainted by all that filth too.

126
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,519
You don't even realize it yourself, do you?

127
00:09:13,639 --> 00:09:14,799
That's just the way the world is.

128
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:18,639
Hardly anyone is purely good.

129
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,080
Neither you nor I could withstand judgment.

130
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,320
Judgment of the law,

131
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,039
judgment of morality,

132
00:09:26,639 --> 00:09:27,639
judgment of conscience.

133
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:36,200
Only when we face judgment

134
00:09:39,799 --> 00:09:41,960
can we truly see the evil within ourselves.

135
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,919
Tomorrow I'll go to the police station.

136
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:58,759
I'll confess to everything.

137
00:13:12,519 --> 00:13:13,080
Sister Xuemei,

138
00:13:15,879 --> 00:13:16,440
wake up.

139
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,320
Haipeng.

140
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:25,720
Take this.

141
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:29,639
Let's go!

142
00:13:29,639 --> 00:13:30,360
Let's go hand out the money!

143
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,440
Let's go.

144
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:32,840
Move it.

145
00:13:42,759 --> 00:13:43,320
Come on!

146
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:45,879
Where is everyone?

147
00:13:46,519 --> 00:13:47,559
Sister Xuemei, come on.

148
00:13:47,799 --> 00:13:48,440
Where's everybody?

149
00:13:50,639 --> 00:13:52,639
Where is everyone? Come on out!

150
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,360
Sister Xuemei is back!

151
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,720
Xuemei's back!

152
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,320
Holy cow!

153
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,279
Xuemei!

154
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:58,879
You're back!

155
00:13:58,879 --> 00:13:59,679
Hurry over here!

156
00:14:02,399 --> 00:14:04,519
Sister Xuemei is handing out money!

157
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,600
Don't push! Stop shoving!

158
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,120
Here.

159
00:14:13,559 --> 00:14:14,080
Holy smokes!

160
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:14,960
There's so much! Here.

161
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,519
This is yours.

162
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:18,799
This is yours.

163
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:19,720
Here you go.

164
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:20,440
Wonderful!

165
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:22,159
This is great!

166
00:14:22,279 --> 00:14:22,879
Awesome!

167
00:14:25,799 --> 00:14:26,399
Fantastic!

168
00:14:26,519 --> 00:14:27,159
This is amazing!

169
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:32,519
Great!

170
00:14:34,279 --> 00:14:35,240
Mine too! Don't forget me!

171
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,240
This is mine!

172
00:14:40,159 --> 00:14:41,000
There's so much!

173
00:16:26,639 --> 00:16:27,039
Over there.

174
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:28,799
Let's go check it out.

175
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,039
Xiaosheng,

176
00:17:14,119 --> 00:17:15,799
This is the first time I've ever written a letter,

177
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:17,799
and it'll be my last.

178
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:20,920
My life is coming to an end.

179
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,119
I used to think I did the right thing

180
00:17:24,519 --> 00:17:25,480
using the wrong methods,

181
00:17:26,759 --> 00:17:27,839
but the truth is, I was just wrong.

182
00:17:28,799 --> 00:17:30,200
If I had known that sooner,

183
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:32,440
maybe I would've made the right choices.

184
00:17:33,799 --> 00:17:34,880
I remember you telling me

185
00:17:35,759 --> 00:17:37,519
that Chen Yuan said your mother's bottle cap

186
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,400
would be one of a kind.

187
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:40,759
So I'm giving it to you

188
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:42,279
as a keepsake.

189
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,359
And another thing...

190
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:46,319
I brought ruin upon my mentor.

191
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,200
One day, when he's released from prison,

192
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,039
I hope you can go pick him up.

193
00:17:52,559 --> 00:17:53,440
If possible,

194
00:17:53,799 --> 00:17:54,839
please look after him for me.

195
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:57,200
Xiaosheng,

196
00:17:58,559 --> 00:17:59,559
everything I did

197
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,480
was utterly foolish.

198
00:18:01,519 --> 00:18:02,440
It destroyed me,

199
00:18:03,079 --> 00:18:04,039
ruined my mentor,

200
00:18:05,079 --> 00:18:06,160
and hurt so many people.

201
00:18:07,599 --> 00:18:09,759
But if it clears your mother's name,

202
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,240
then it was worth it.

203
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,519
Right now, I want to tell you:

204
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,680
Even though this world is full of evil and injustice,

205
00:18:18,359 --> 00:18:19,720
we can't become criminals.

206
00:18:20,319 --> 00:18:21,720
You must be a good person,

207
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,559
just like your mother was.

208
00:18:24,079 --> 00:18:24,839
Kind,

209
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:25,920
upright,

210
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:26,799
forbearing,

211
00:18:27,279 --> 00:18:27,839
and compassionate.

212
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,400
It's not easy.

213
00:18:30,839 --> 00:18:31,759
None of us could manage it.

214
00:18:32,519 --> 00:18:33,279
Now it's up to you.

215
00:18:34,559 --> 00:18:34,960
Wishing you

216
00:18:35,799 --> 00:18:36,680
all the best,

217
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:37,880
Liu Tieping

218
00:19:03,839 --> 00:19:04,880
The house is sold.

219
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:08,799
When are you moving?

220
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,400
As soon as I can.

221
00:19:11,759 --> 00:19:13,079
So you won't get annoyed seeing me.

222
00:19:13,839 --> 00:19:14,440
First thing in the morning,

223
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,680
what did I do to tick you off?

224
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,359
No, no, nothing like that.

225
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:19,599
It's just...

226
00:19:21,039 --> 00:19:22,039
I just feel a bit...

227
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:27,200
Don't tell me you're gonna miss me.

228
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:30,599
Hold on a sec.

229
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:31,960
What is it?

230
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:41,480
What's this?

231
00:19:43,119 --> 00:19:44,400
I pulled this from The Malt Kingdom,

232
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,599
picked it out frame by frame.

233
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,759
Since you're leaving,

234
00:19:48,559 --> 00:19:49,240
keep it as a keepsake.

235
00:20:14,519 --> 00:20:15,279
What a beauty.

236
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,079
Who's that?

237
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,200
Smiling so happily.

238
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,680
This is the best photo

239
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:34,039
taken of me in my whole life.

240
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,400
Thank you.

241
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:47,039
By the way,

242
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:48,480
there's something

243
00:20:48,759 --> 00:20:50,240
I've been too embarrassed to tell you.

244
00:20:51,319 --> 00:20:53,160
I've always thought you're really talented.

245
00:20:56,359 --> 00:20:58,359
Keep making good films in the future.

246
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:00,960
Just make the kind

247
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,240
that's real,

248
00:21:04,039 --> 00:21:05,119
that moves people,

249
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,880
the kind that gives people strength.

250
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:08,759
You know what I mean?

251
00:21:10,079 --> 00:21:11,599
Who even watches that stuff anymore?

252
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,200
I'm thinking of

253
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,000
getting laid off.

254
00:21:22,279 --> 00:21:23,359
Get outta here!

255
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,400
If you get laid off,

256
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,599
I don't even deserve to live.

257
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,920
Just messing with you.

258
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:32,880
I'll keep filming.

259
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:41,400
Your hands are pretty rough, huh?

260
00:21:43,039 --> 00:21:44,400
The hands that hold a camera

261
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,559
aren't any better than mine that rub feet.

262
00:22:05,079 --> 00:22:07,319
Take good care of yourself, okay?

263
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:11,960
You take care too.

264
00:22:17,559 --> 00:22:18,119
Goodbye.

265
00:22:25,559 --> 00:22:26,640
By the way, Shen Leshui.

266
00:22:27,559 --> 00:22:28,240
Well...

267
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,200
Cheng Youtian had someone

268
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,519
give me the keys to Old Workers' Haven.

269
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,359
He asked me to go by when I have time

270
00:22:34,359 --> 00:22:35,599
and help clean the place up.

271
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:37,200
Why don't the two of us go together?

272
00:22:39,319 --> 00:22:40,839
If it weren't for Director Cheng that day,

273
00:22:41,559 --> 00:22:42,519
I'd be dead.

274
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,359
How about noon the day after tomorrow?

275
00:22:49,039 --> 00:22:50,039
The day after tomorrow?

276
00:22:51,279 --> 00:22:52,319
Can't we do today?

277
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:54,599
Let's make it the day after tomorrow.

278
00:22:55,319 --> 00:22:56,359
All right. What time then?

279
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:58,720
11:30.

280
00:22:59,000 --> 00:22:59,519
Okay.

281
00:23:00,319 --> 00:23:01,599
See you at Old Workers' Haven.

282
00:23:09,559 --> 00:23:10,039
Bye.

283
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:13,440
Bye.

284
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:32,240
What is all this junk?

285
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:32,680
Looks like

286
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,039
a junk collector's dump.

287
00:23:35,319 --> 00:23:36,119
The place is sold.

288
00:23:36,119 --> 00:23:37,599
They're coming to renovate in a couple of days.

289
00:23:38,279 --> 00:23:39,759
I brought you some things

290
00:23:39,759 --> 00:23:41,240
so you don't call me wasteful.

291
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:42,880
I can't stand it.

292
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:54,720
You're all grown up now.

293
00:23:56,559 --> 00:23:57,640
So what are you going to do now?

294
00:23:59,079 --> 00:24:01,039
You've got hands, feet, and a brain.

295
00:24:01,039 --> 00:24:02,200
A whole bright future ahead.

296
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,319
You're wheezing so hard.

297
00:24:06,079 --> 00:24:06,599
I'm fine.

298
00:24:06,599 --> 00:24:07,480
Let me listen. Let me listen.

299
00:24:14,519 --> 00:24:15,599
Your heartbeat...

300
00:24:15,599 --> 00:24:16,839
It's beating so strongly.

301
00:24:17,559 --> 00:24:18,400
It sounds wonderful.

302
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:21,640
Of course.

303
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,039
Getting in the right mindset

304
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:27,759
was so crucial.

305
00:24:29,039 --> 00:24:30,920
We did the right thing.

306
00:24:33,559 --> 00:24:35,240
In this warm heartbeat,

307
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:37,599
I feel like I can hear your voice.

308
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:40,480
Thank you, Sister Xuemei.

309
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:42,799
Your wish...

310
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:44,759
I'll fulfill it for you.

311
00:24:50,759 --> 00:24:51,279
Give it to me.

312
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,039
Thanks.

313
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:57,200
Got all your things?

314
00:24:58,160 --> 00:24:59,160
Keep your ID safe.

315
00:25:01,839 --> 00:25:02,319
Once you

316
00:25:02,759 --> 00:25:03,720
head off to big Beijing,

317
00:25:04,079 --> 00:25:06,440
visit our little Lacheng when you're free.

318
00:25:07,599 --> 00:25:08,960
Come hang out with me on your vacation!

319
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,240
How would I dare go there?

320
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:11,079
Beijing is so huge.

321
00:25:11,079 --> 00:25:11,880
What if I get lost?

322
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:16,039
What's with you?

323
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:17,759
Why are you acting so shy?

324
00:25:18,359 --> 00:25:19,480
You're both single,

325
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,559
and you were middle school deskmates.

326
00:25:20,559 --> 00:25:21,680
What's there to be shy about?

327
00:25:21,839 --> 00:25:22,599
Cut the nonsense.

328
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:24,640
The two of us

329
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,200
weren't deskmates.

330
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,000
Front and back row.

331
00:25:27,519 --> 00:25:28,480
Xiao Gao isn't talking nonsense.

332
00:25:28,759 --> 00:25:29,599
You're just taking it the wrong way.

333
00:25:30,799 --> 00:25:31,839
Did I take it the wrong way?

334
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:32,920
Look at you...

335
00:25:34,079 --> 00:25:34,680
Director Shen.

336
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,279
Wait, Chief Editor Shen.

337
00:25:36,359 --> 00:25:37,160
Reporter Shen.

338
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,119
Why do you have so many titles?

339
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:40,920
What do you actually do?

340
00:25:41,279 --> 00:25:42,039
You have no fixed address,

341
00:25:42,039 --> 00:25:42,880
and so many titles.

342
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,200
You could easily become

343
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,640
a person of interest for us.

344
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,960
Got a place to stay back in Beijing?

345
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,440
Beijing is so expensive,

346
00:25:50,640 --> 00:25:51,720
and so crowded.

347
00:25:52,119 --> 00:25:53,000
At your age,

348
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:53,839
would anyone even want you?

349
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:56,319
What did you say?

350
00:25:57,079 --> 00:25:58,759
Nobody wants you!

351
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:00,640
Look at all your wrinkles.

352
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:01,480
You even have gray hair.

353
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:02,240
Impossible.

354
00:26:02,359 --> 00:26:03,720
He just plucked them for me yesterday.

355
00:26:04,839 --> 00:26:05,759
You're supposed to pluck the gray ones, man!

356
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:07,920
You didn't say to pluck the gray ones!

357
00:26:08,079 --> 00:26:09,200
So you plucked the black ones?!

358
00:26:09,839 --> 00:26:10,839
All right, cut it out.

359
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:15,000
Look at you, all grown up,

360
00:26:15,359 --> 00:26:16,519
and you can't even spit it out.

361
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:17,319
I'll say it for you.

362
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,079
Classmate Shen Leshui,

363
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,279
From the first time I saw you,

364
00:26:23,279 --> 00:26:23,960
I liked you.

365
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:25,559
Through all three years of middle school,

366
00:26:25,559 --> 00:26:26,759
I always stared at your back.

367
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,640
Now at our age,

368
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:29,960
you're unmarried and so am I.

369
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,039
Could we maybe just slip up

370
00:26:32,039 --> 00:26:32,839
and grow old together?

371
00:26:32,839 --> 00:26:33,759
Could... could you...

372
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:34,960
Give me a break!

373
00:26:35,359 --> 00:26:36,079
What are you doing?

374
00:26:36,599 --> 00:26:38,319
D-Don't listen to his nonsense!

375
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:40,319
It's fine, really.

376
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:41,799
I don't feel that way either.

377
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:44,599
You, though...

378
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:46,000
take good care of yourself.

379
00:26:46,279 --> 00:26:47,200
Stay safe.

380
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,240
Text me when you're free.

381
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:50,079
Keep in touch.

382
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:51,960
Sure, don't worry.

383
00:26:52,559 --> 00:26:53,480
If I text you,

384
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,640
make sure to reply!

385
00:27:00,359 --> 00:27:01,039
Take care.

386
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:01,839
Sister Leshui,

387
00:27:02,559 --> 00:27:03,680
sorry for all the trouble.

388
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,200
Thank you.

389
00:27:07,599 --> 00:27:08,759
Say hello to Grandma for me.

390
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,279
Keep up your in-depth reporting.

391
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:15,880
Do a poor job, and I'll disown you.

392
00:27:17,039 --> 00:27:17,920
You do your best, too.

393
00:27:18,279 --> 00:27:19,559
Do a poor job, and I'll disown you too.

394
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:22,039
Safe travels.

395
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:24,720
Take care.

396
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:31,599
Did you freeze up?

397
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:36,880
Come here.

398
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:38,680
Student Han Chuang.

399
00:27:39,599 --> 00:27:40,200
What?

400
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:41,359
Officer Han.

401
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:42,480
Keep it up.

402
00:27:42,799 --> 00:27:45,680
W-Wait, why do I get treated differently?

403
00:27:50,559 --> 00:27:51,759
You take care of yourself too.

404
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,960
Look after yourself back in Beijing.

405
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:56,079
If there's ever anything...

406
00:27:56,079 --> 00:27:56,960
...troubling you... The car's here.

407
00:27:58,519 --> 00:27:59,200
I'm freezing.

408
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:00,000
Take care.

409
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:01,720
I'm off.

410
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:03,000
Take care.

411
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:03,720
Take care.

412
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:05,200
Take care.

413
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:06,240
Take care.

414
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:07,200
I'm off.

415
00:28:31,079 --> 00:28:31,759
Come on!

416
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:17,680
Alright.

417
00:29:18,319 --> 00:29:19,240
Quite the fortune cat, huh?

418
00:29:20,799 --> 00:29:22,079
This classmate of mine...

419
00:29:22,279 --> 00:29:23,079
has really had it rough.

420
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:31,519
We've still got a job to do.

421
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:32,359
Let's go.

422
00:29:53,119 --> 00:29:53,720
Hello.

423
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:56,079
Is this Old Workers' Haven?

424
00:29:56,279 --> 00:29:56,680
Yeah.

425
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,759
Shen Leshui told me to be here at 11:30 AM

426
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:03,319
to look for a Ms. Tu Chunyan.

427
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:06,039
I'm Tu Chunyan.

428
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:09,400
Shen Leshui also asked me

429
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,200
to meet her here at this time.

430
00:30:10,480 --> 00:30:11,160
Where is she?

431
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:12,839
I have no idea where she went either.

432
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:16,599
This Shen Leshui...

433
00:30:16,759 --> 00:30:17,519
She set up a meeting and didn't even show up.

434
00:30:17,519 --> 00:30:18,960
What's she pulling here?

435
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:21,039
Who are you, anyway?

436
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:22,559
I'm Liu Xiaosheng.

437
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,240
Liu Xuemei's son.

438
00:30:37,680 --> 00:30:38,880
It's from Shen Leshui.

439
00:30:48,519 --> 00:30:49,720
Chun... Chun...

440
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:50,279
Sister Chunyan...

441
00:30:51,359 --> 00:30:52,559
My mom is innocent.

442
00:30:54,559 --> 00:30:55,279
Is it here? I...

443
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:55,759
I...

444
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,720
My mom...

445
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:01,039
My mom is innocent.

446
00:31:04,039 --> 00:31:04,839
She's innocent.

447
00:31:15,839 --> 00:31:16,359
Whoa.

448
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,359
What's this supposed to mean?

449
00:31:41,759 --> 00:31:43,039
Where did all this money come from?

450
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,000
My mom's bag.

451
00:31:49,359 --> 00:31:50,519
This is Shen Leshui's money.

452
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:51,640
Exactly 200,000.

453
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:53,880
She asked me to make sure it gets to both of you.

454
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:56,279
Here's the receipt.

455
00:32:00,839 --> 00:32:02,039
This is Shen Leshui's

456
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:03,599
money from selling her house.

457
00:32:06,880 --> 00:32:07,880
Please sign for it.

458
00:32:10,559 --> 00:32:11,880
Here, Xiaosheng.

459
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:37,720
Bro,

460
00:32:44,359 --> 00:32:45,519
where did Shen Leshui go?

461
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:48,480
She went back to Beijing.

462
00:33:12,920 --> 00:33:14,119
Dear Xiaosheng,

463
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:15,640
Chunyan,

464
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,720
it's Shen Leshui.

465
00:33:18,559 --> 00:33:20,279
I had to leave early this morning,

466
00:33:20,839 --> 00:33:21,960
so I am counting on you both.

467
00:33:22,799 --> 00:33:24,000
Please help me

468
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,000
read this letter to everyone.

469
00:33:26,519 --> 00:33:27,599
All this time,

470
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:29,640
I've been trying to find out

471
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:31,279
what happened to Liu Xuemei's money.

472
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:34,720
Now, there is finally conclusive proof.

473
00:33:35,079 --> 00:33:35,759
Therefore,

474
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:37,440
I can state with certainty that

475
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:40,359
Liu Xuemei was innocent.

476
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:45,920
Over a decade ago,

477
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,240
Liu Xuemei

478
00:33:47,279 --> 00:33:50,039
was blocked outside the auction by Ma Guowen,

479
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:51,839
deliberately forced to drink,

480
00:33:52,279 --> 00:33:53,720
and died of hypothermia.

481
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,559
With her very life,

482
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:59,559
she recovered the money that belonged to the fellow workers.

483
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:02,599
Regrettably,

484
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:04,720
the truth

485
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:06,799
only came to light

486
00:34:06,799 --> 00:34:08,000
more than a decade after her death.

487
00:34:09,039 --> 00:34:09,960
This 200,000 yuan...

488
00:34:10,719 --> 00:34:12,800
Liu Xuemei originally wanted to give it to those

489
00:34:13,039 --> 00:34:14,440
who pooled funds to buy the factory,

490
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:17,239
yet were afraid to step forward to reclaim it,

491
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:19,440
as well as

492
00:34:19,719 --> 00:34:20,679
those fellow workers facing hardships

493
00:34:20,880 --> 00:34:22,559
and in need of help.

494
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:26,000
I've asked Officer Gao Xuelin

495
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:27,360
to deliver this long-overdue gesture

496
00:34:27,599 --> 00:34:28,599
to all of you.

497
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:33,400
Please handle these funds

498
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:35,159
according to Liu Xuemei's wishes,

499
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:39,440
and pass on her kindness and sincerity

500
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,199
to everyone.

501
00:34:46,519 --> 00:34:48,880
She was a noble woman,

502
00:34:50,679 --> 00:34:52,360
a decent soul full of love and integrity,

503
00:34:54,719 --> 00:34:56,320
and a friend worthy of being remembered.

504
00:34:58,119 --> 00:34:58,760
In addition,

505
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:00,719
I want to pay tribute to every fellow worker

506
00:35:00,719 --> 00:35:02,920
who took part in the factory buyout back then,

507
00:35:03,639 --> 00:35:05,440
as well as all the fellow workers

508
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:07,599
who were laid off in Ma Guowen's retaliation.

509
00:35:07,880 --> 00:35:08,519
I salute you all.

510
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:16,440
Your kindness,

511
00:35:17,119 --> 00:35:17,840
optimism,

512
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:19,599
and love for life

513
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:23,400
meant that in your hardest, most painful,

514
00:35:23,559 --> 00:35:24,840
and loneliest times,

515
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:27,239
you never forgot to strive hard

516
00:35:27,639 --> 00:35:28,599
and help one another.

517
00:35:29,639 --> 00:35:30,440
I am deeply sorry

518
00:35:31,159 --> 00:35:32,880
that back then, I failed to publish

519
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:35,199
the truth about your struggle.

520
00:35:35,639 --> 00:35:37,920
I ask for your forgiveness here and now.

521
00:35:40,239 --> 00:35:41,639
I also want to tell you:

522
00:35:42,039 --> 00:35:43,119
what happened in the past

523
00:35:43,639 --> 00:35:45,039
is now history.

524
00:35:45,679 --> 00:35:47,800
Always remember those days of fighting together.

525
00:35:48,639 --> 00:35:50,880
A brighter tomorrow surely awaits us.

526
00:35:56,599 --> 00:35:57,360
Th-This... This...

527
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,480
This is the 200,000 yuan!

528
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:08,079
Liu Xuemei was innocent!

529
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:10,639
Xiaosheng,

530
00:36:11,519 --> 00:36:12,639
your mother was innocent!

531
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:16,239
My mother was innocent!

532
00:36:18,079 --> 00:36:19,239
She was a good person!

533
00:36:21,039 --> 00:36:22,559
She never betrayed your trust!

534
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,639
Sister Xuemei,

535
00:37:32,599 --> 00:37:33,719
I really can't think of

536
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:35,760
a better way to honor your memory,

537
00:37:36,679 --> 00:37:37,679
so let's all

538
00:37:38,519 --> 00:37:39,760
drink till we drop with you.

539
00:38:02,039 --> 00:38:02,920
Hello, everyone.

540
00:38:03,159 --> 00:38:04,760
My name is Sun Jianguo.

541
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,440
I'm 40 this year.

542
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:08,159
I've been working at this factory

543
00:38:08,159 --> 00:38:10,199
for 22 years now.

544
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:12,840
I've been very happy here.

545
00:38:13,199 --> 00:38:15,199
Every day feels fulfilling.

546
00:38:15,679 --> 00:38:16,719
My name is Li Dongyuan.

547
00:38:16,960 --> 00:38:18,400
I'm 32 years old.

548
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,719
I have a three-year-old son.

549
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,239
I work here.

550
00:38:22,599 --> 00:38:24,000
I love Lacheng Brewery.

551
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:25,360
Lacheng Brewery is my home.

552
00:38:25,760 --> 00:38:27,159
My name is Ge Shun.

553
00:38:27,239 --> 00:38:28,559
I'm 35 years old.

554
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:29,960
At Lacheng Brewery,

555
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:31,960
I've worked for 15 years.

556
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:33,320
Working here,

557
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:35,039
I feel honored and proud.

558
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:37,559
As for my dream,

559
00:38:37,760 --> 00:38:39,519
work hard, make more money,

560
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,280
so my wife and son

561
00:38:41,400 --> 00:38:43,079
can live a good life.

562
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:44,159
Next up,

563
00:39:06,199 --> 00:39:07,280
At the end of 1999,

564
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:09,639
the auction of Lacheng Brewery

565
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,519
was a turning point for many fellow workers.

566
00:39:13,599 --> 00:39:15,440
It held both passion and struggle,

567
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:17,519
as well as silence and betrayal.

568
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:19,800
Regrettably,

569
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,559
the documentary The Malt Kingdom back then,

570
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,239
under pressure from various sides,

571
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:27,079
failed to capture the full picture of the event.

572
00:39:28,599 --> 00:39:30,239
The intention behind The New Malt Kingdom

573
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:33,320
is to offer the fellow workers caught in it

574
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:37,519
a belated tribute and apology.

575
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:39,599
Here, there's not only

576
00:39:39,599 --> 00:39:41,039
the journey of their past struggles,

577
00:39:41,559 --> 00:39:43,519
but also their unyielding resistance.

578
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:45,880
The New Malt Kingdom

579
00:39:46,199 --> 00:39:48,519
will present the whole story from start to finish.

580
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:52,079
Their stories deserve to be seen.

581
00:39:52,920 --> 00:39:53,960
Their lives

582
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:56,039
deserve to be recorded.

583
00:39:57,119 --> 00:39:58,159
Some say

584
00:39:58,519 --> 00:39:59,920
under the shadow of the internet,

585
00:40:00,599 --> 00:40:02,280
the line between truth and falsehood

586
00:40:02,559 --> 00:40:03,800
grows harder and harder to discern.

587
00:40:04,880 --> 00:40:07,760
Traditional media will inevitably be left behind,

588
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:09,719
and news that reflects the facts

589
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:11,320
will ultimately be replaced

590
00:40:11,320 --> 00:40:13,400
by one sensational headline after another.

591
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:16,239
But as a journalist,

592
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:17,800
what I want to record

593
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:20,199
are real people

594
00:40:20,639 --> 00:40:21,639
and real events.

595
00:40:23,440 --> 00:40:26,480
The truth is often fragmented and complex,

596
00:40:27,119 --> 00:40:29,119
accompanied by discordant noise.

597
00:40:30,159 --> 00:40:31,400
Yet precisely because of this,

598
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:34,719
the laughter and tears

599
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:36,519
become all the more precious.

600
00:40:38,079 --> 00:40:39,159
Even today,

601
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,159
I still remember

602
00:40:41,639 --> 00:40:42,840
those youthful,

603
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,480
vibrant faces I saw back then,

604
00:40:45,119 --> 00:40:47,119
and those spirited vows.

605
00:40:48,679 --> 00:40:50,199
Though times have changed,

606
00:40:51,079 --> 00:40:52,639
and many who lived through it

607
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,599
have gone from their prime

608
00:40:55,079 --> 00:40:56,519
to silver-haired elders,

609
00:40:57,719 --> 00:40:58,840
while some

610
00:40:59,599 --> 00:41:00,920
have already passed away,

611
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:03,360
I hope these memories

612
00:41:04,079 --> 00:41:06,199
will become part of history,

613
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:08,840
remembered forever.

614
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,280
Time is a cure,

615
00:41:11,639 --> 00:41:12,840
and also a cup of mellow wine.

616
00:41:13,599 --> 00:41:15,079
Tempered through the years,

617
00:41:15,679 --> 00:41:16,840
its fragrance only deepens.

618
00:41:18,159 --> 00:41:20,199
Let us open the gates of the Malt Kingdom,

619
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:22,719
and in this golden land,

620
00:41:23,119 --> 00:41:24,199
dream together

621
00:41:24,599 --> 00:41:26,480
a grand, beer-scented dream.

622
00:41:28,519 --> 00:41:29,800
These final words,

623
00:41:30,639 --> 00:41:31,639
I write to myself:

624
00:41:33,559 --> 00:41:34,320
Shen Leshui,

625
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,199
ever since you graduated from college,

626
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:38,960
you wanted to be a journalist,

627
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:40,920
to report the truth,

628
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,440
care about life,

629
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:45,480
and record ordinary people's joys and sorrows.

630
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,599
Though there were wasted years and regrets,

631
00:41:49,039 --> 00:41:49,800
I still hope

632
00:41:50,039 --> 00:41:52,239
you'll never forget your ideals.

633
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:55,599
Don't let life smooth away your edges.

634
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:59,239
Don't let the years halt your steps.

635
00:42:00,199 --> 00:42:01,760
When you grow old

636
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:04,159
and look back on your life,

637
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,360
may you proudly say:

638
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,119
"I was here."

639
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:10,519
Hello,

640
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,159
Shen Leshui.

641
00:42:13,320 --> 00:42:14,199
Hello.
